<title>NEW ZEALAND: RBNZ sees 1.5 pct inflation as &quot;aiming point&quot;.</title>
<headline>RBNZ sees 1.5 pct inflation as &quot;aiming point&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Reserve Bank governor Don Brash said the move to target inflation in a 0-3 percent band from 0-2 percent meant a small change to the bank's &quot;aiming point&quot; to 1.5 percent from 1.0 percent.</p>
<p>The change was made as part of the coalition deal between the conservative National Party and the nationalist New Zealand First Party announced last week.</p>
<p>&quot;We will assuredly not be content with projecting inflation at or close to three percent,&quot; Brash said.</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom (64-4-4734746)</p>
</text>
